<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>出版物 |皮尤研究中心</title><link>https://www.pewresearch.org/publications/</link><description>塑造您世界的数字、事实和趋势</description><lastBuildDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 15:48:36 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>在全球范围内，更多的人预计人工智能会导致失业而不是增长</title><link>https://www.pewresearch.org/global/2026/09/17/globally-more-people-expect-ai-to-cause-job-loss-than-growth/</link><description>&lt;img height="110" src="https://www.pewresearch.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/20/2026/09/PG_26.09.17_GlobalViewsOfAI_featured@2x.png?w=194&amp;amp;h=110&amp;amp;crop=1" width="194" /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;p&gt;对人工智能的担忧和兴奋交织在一起，一项针对 37 个国家的调查发现，人们对其对就业和经济不平等的潜在影响持悲观态度。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt; &lt;span style="font-size: 12px; color: gray;"&gt;（使用&lt;a href="https://fetchrss.com/feedLink?w=6a6d836405e2f22d650b3382" target="_blank"&gt;FetchRSS&lt;/a&gt;生成的提要）&lt;/span&gt;</description><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 15:48:36 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.pewresearch.org/global/2026/09/17/globally-more-people-expect-ai-to-cause-job-loss-than-growth/</guid></item><item><title>民主党人现在比共和党人更担心人工智能及其对就业的影响</title><link>https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2026/09/16/democrats-are-now-more-worried-than-republicans-about-ai-and-its-impact-on-jobs/</link><description>&lt;img height="110" src="https://www.pewresearch.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/20/2026/09/SR_09.16_26_ai-partisan-views_crop.png?w=194&amp;amp;h=110&amp;amp;crop=1" width="194" /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;p&gt;另一个转变是，民主党人现在比共和党人更有可能预测人工智能将在未来 20 年导致就业机会减少（75% 对 68%）。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt; &lt;span style="font-size: 12px; color: gray;"&gt;（使用&lt;a href="https://fetchrss.com/feedLink?w=6a6d836405e2f22d650b3382" target="_blank"&gt;FetchRSS&lt;/a&gt;生成的提要）&lt;/span&gt;</description><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 15:48:36 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2026/09/16/democrats-are-now-more-worried-than-republicans-about-ai-and-its-impact-on-jobs/</guid></item><item><title>对政党归属和过去投票进行加权民意调查</title><link>https://www.pewresearch.org/methods/2026/09/16/weighting-polls-on-party-affiliation-and-past-vote/</link><description>&lt;img height="110" src="https://www.pewresearch.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/20/2026/09/PM_2026.9.16_party-weighting_crop.png?w=194&amp;amp;h=110&amp;amp;crop=1" width="194" /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;p&gt;本报告解释了政治权重的运作方式、皮尤研究中心的运作方式及其一些局限性。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt; &lt;span style="font-size: 12px; color: gray;"&gt;（使用&lt;a href="https://fetchrss.com/feedLink?w=6a6d836405e2f22d650b3382" target="_blank"&gt;FetchRSS&lt;/a&gt;生成的提要）&lt;/span&gt;</description><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 15:48:36 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.pewresearch.org/methods/2026/09/16/weighting-polls-on-party-affiliation-and-past-vote/</guid></item><item><title>2026 年初选季选举前众议院更替率达到 30 多年来最高水平</title><link>https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2026/09/16/2026-primary-season-yields-greatest-preelection-house-turnover-in-over-3-decades/</link><description>&lt;img height="110" src="https://www.pewresearch.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/20/2026/09/SR_26.09.16_house-incumbent_featured.jpg?w=194&amp;amp;h=110&amp;amp;crop=1" width="194" /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;p&gt; 74 名众议院议员不会重返下届国会，这一数字比 1992 年以来的任何一次大选之前的人数都要多。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt; &lt;span style="font-size: 12px; color: gray;"&gt;（使用&lt;a href="https://fetchrss.com/feedLink?w=6a6d836405e2f22d650b3382" target="_blank"&gt;FetchRSS&lt;/a&gt;生成的提要）&lt;/span&gt;</description><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 15:48:36 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2026/09/16/2026-primary-season-yields-greatest-preelection-house-turnover-in-over-3-decades/</guid></item><item><title>许多以色列人和巴勒斯坦人表示他们无法和平共处 - 并解释原因</title><link>https://www.pewresearch.org/global/2026/09/15/many-israelis-and-palestinians-say-they-cannot-coexist-peacefully-and-explain-why/</link><description>&lt;img height="110" src="https://www.pewresearch.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/20/2026/09/PG_26.09.15_Coexistance_featured@2x.png?w=194&amp;amp;h=110&amp;amp;crop=1" width="194" /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;p&gt;西岸和东耶路撒冷的以色列人和巴勒斯坦人反思两国解决方案的可行性&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12px; color: gray;"&gt;（使用&lt;a href="https://fetchrss.com/feedLink?w=6a6d836405e2f22d650b3382" target="_blank"&gt;FetchRSS&lt;/a&gt;生成的提要）&lt;/span&gt;</description><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 15:41:59 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.pewresearch.org/global/2026/09/15/many-israelis-and-palestinians-say-they-cannot-coexist-peacefully-and-explain-why/</guid></item></channel></rss>